// zig/raw-loan's wire type -- deliberately minimal (a bare sequence number),
// unkeyed, single instance, same discipline as hello_world/presence. The
// payload is incidental; what matters is that the publisher/subscriber
// bypass TypeSupport marshaling entirely and go through the raw/loaned
// DataWriter/DataReader operations (loan_raw/publish_loan_raw/take_raw/
// return_loan_raw) directly. See docs/design/raw-loan-reference-app.md at
// the repo root for the full spec. Byte-identical copy required in
// c/raw-loan, cpp/raw-loan, java/raw-loan once those ports exist (same
// discipline hello_world.idl already follows across bindings).
@appendable
struct LoanedPing {
    int32 seq_num;
};
